---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About CityClick — Municipal Intelligence"
  description="CityClick is an independent municipal intelligence platform providing sourced municipal data for travelers, relocating families, and business founders."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="space-y-4 mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-[#1D68F2] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
        <span>🏛️</span> Our Mission
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-[#152438] tracking-tight">
        Sourced data for your next city.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        CityClick exists to eliminate the guesswork, algorithmic fog, and outdated blogs that surround exploring, moving to, or doing business in American cities.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-[#152438]">Why We Built CityClick</h2>
        <p>
          Whether you are a weekend visitor booking flights, a family evaluating school districts and property tax burdens, or an entrepreneur underwriting commercial lease breakeven across 25 NAICS trades, you deserve facts backed by audited provenance—not sponsored clickbait.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most city sites are either tourist marketing boards hiding practical drawbacks or clinical Census spreadsheets that normal humans cannot parse. CityClick bridges the gap: authentic visual orientation (4K drone tours, street-level photography) paired with audited institutional data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-[#152438]">Our Sourcing Standard</h2>
        <p>
          Every metric displayed on CityClick—from municipal water potability (PWSID) and USGS 3DEP elevation contours to ad-valorem millage rates and Federal Reserve FRED economic indices—is anchored to official public records.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200">
            <div class="font-black text-sm text-[#152438] mb-1">✈️ For Visitors</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">Airport transit reality, rideshare levels, drinking water safety, curated district stays, and arrival protocols.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200">
            <div class="font-black text-sm text-[#152438] mb-1">🏡 For Movers</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">True property tax millage, public school zones, municipal utility setup, and neighborhood cost comparisons.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#F8FAFC] border border-slate-200">
            <div class="font-black text-sm text-[#152438] mb-1">💼 For Business</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600">25-NAICS trade density, Census ZBP counts, NNN commercial lease benchmarks, and municipal permit queues.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-[#152438]">Independent & Free Public Access</h2>
        <p>
          We do not gate essential civic information behind paywalls. Our institutional feasibility dossiers, visitor pocket guides, and relocation checklists are 100% free public resources designed to empower everyday citizens, founders, and visitors.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3.5 rounded-2xl bg-[#1D68F2] hover:bg-[#1555C7] text-white font-bold text-xs shadow-md transition">
            Explore 1,501 Published City Guides →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
